<title>USA: Deere to sell farm equipment to Kazakhstan.</title>
<headline>Deere to sell farm equipment to Kazakhstan.</headline>
<dateline>MOLINE, Ill. 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deere &amp; Co said Tuesday it sold $114 million worth of agricultural equipment to the Central Asian republic of Kazakhstan.</p>
<p>The deal includes 630 combine harvesters, 100 cotton pickers and other related equipment. Delivery is scheduled to begin next year.</p>
<p>It's the second largest transaction in the agricultural equipment maker's history, according to a Deere spokesman. The Moline-based company sold 1,049 combines to the Ukraine earlier this year. - Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
